GPU: hardware compositing on Apple silicon without Dawn.

On arm64 Macs Chromium's only hardware mode is Graphite, on Dawn, which the
slim profile leaves out for size (docs/SIZE_AND_SPEED.md). With neither, the
GPU modes were display compositor alone: every page composited in software, on
a machine with a Metal GPU, seen on a Mac as chrome://gpu's gpu_compositing:
disabled_software, while WebGL ran on Metal through ANGLE. Skia's GL back end on
that same ANGLE is the mode Chromium still has for Intel Macs; it is in the
build already, and this costs no size.

--- a/content/browser/gpu/gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc
+++ b/content/browser/gpu/gpu_data_manager_impl_private.cc
@@ -433,9 +433,8 @@ class HDRProxy {
 
 GpuDataManagerImplPrivate::GpuDataManagerImplPrivate(GpuDataManagerImpl* owner)
     : owner_(owner),
-#if BUILDFLAG(IS_MAC)
-      supports_gpu_mode_hardware_gl_(false),
-#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
+// zebkit: on arm64 Macs too: without Dawn there is no Graphite, and GL on ANGLE's Metal draws.
+#if BUILDFLAG(IS_ANDROID)
       supports_gpu_mode_hardware_gl_(
           !base::FeatureList::IsEnabled(features::kSkipVulkanBlocklist)),
 #else
